# raggo CODEOWNERS — Phase 2.
#
# GitHub looks for CODEOWNERS in `.github/`, the repository root, and
# `docs/`, in that order, and uses the first one it finds. This file
# lives in `.github/` so it takes precedence over the older root-level
# `CODEOWNERS` and is the single source of truth for review routing.
#
# Branch protection on the default branch requires CODEOWNERS review
# for the paths called out in `docs/branch-protection.md` (Phase 2 /
# Phase 3 / Phase 7 prep). Order matters: the LAST matching pattern
# wins, so the catch-all at the top is overridden by more specific
# rules below.

# ---- Default fallback ------------------------------------------------------
*                              @h3ow3d

# ---- Helm chart (Phase 4) --------------------------------------------------
/helm/                         @h3ow3d

# ---- Air-gap bundle (Phase 5) ---------------------------------------------
# The phase plan refers to this directory as `bundle/`; the in-tree
# implementation lives at `airgap-bundle/`. Both paths are covered so
# that a future rename does not silently lose the CODEOWNERS rule.
/bundle/                       @h3ow3d
/airgap-bundle/                @h3ow3d

# ---- CI/CD workflows -------------------------------------------------------
/.github/workflows/            @h3ow3d

# ---- Domain packs (Phase 3 / Phase 7 prep) --------------------------------
/backend/app/domains/          @h3ow3d
